To force a text field to display text in columns using Adobe's JavaScript-based tools, you would typically use a combination of HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Adobe's products like Adobe XD, Adobe Illustrator, or Adobe Photoshop don't have a built-in JavaScript function to directly manipulate text fields in a web page. However, if you're working with a web page and want to create a text field that displays text in columns, you can use HTML and CSS.

Here's an example of how you can achieve this:

HTML:
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Text Field in Columns</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
</head>
<body>
  <div class="text-container">
    <input type="text" id="textField" placeholder="Type here...">
  </div>
  <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

CSS (styles.css):
```css
.text-container {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
  height: 100vh;
}

#textField {
  width: 300px;
  height: 100px;
  font-size: 16px;
  border: 1px solid #ccc;
  padding: 5px;
  overflow: hidden;
  white-space: pre-wrap; /* or 'pre' for no wrapping */
  word-wrap: break-word; /* for long words */
}
```

JavaScript (script.js):
```javascript
// JavaScript can be used to add interactivity or manipulate the text field further if needed.
```

In this example, the text field is styled to have a fixed width and height, and the `white-space: pre-wrap;` CSS property allows the text to wrap within the confines of the text field, effectively creating a column-like appearance. The `word-wrap: break-word;` property ensures that long words will break and wrap to the next line.

If you need to dynamically insert text into the text field and have it display in columns, you can use JavaScript to set the value of the text field. However, the column effect will still be determined by the CSS properties mentioned above.

Please note that this is a simple example and may need to be adjusted based on your specific requirements, such as the number of columns, the width of each column, and the overall layout.

