        printf("Operation succeeded.\n");
    } else if (result == ERROR_OUT_OF_MEMORY) {
        printf("Error: Out of memory.\n");
    } else {
        printf("An unknown error occurred.\n");
    }

    return 0;
}
```

In this example, `performOperation` returns `ERROR_OUT_OF_MEMORY` if it fails. The `main` function checks the return value and handles the error accordingly. This is a simple and widely used pattern in C for error handling.

